# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the window-WY probe's card step (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the integration branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (the tag numbers are the driver's, on the
# allowlist). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the card is resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# NON-EXACT RESEARCH PROBE (docs/gdn-wy-probe.md): no verdict of this job licenses serving, and the window form is never in a serving or traffic profile.
# ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-wy-probe-1 is a PLACEHOLDER the driver substitutes with the combined window's fresh tag; the harness mounts this checkout's scripts, so any
# current C2 image carries the runtime it needs and no build is specific to this probe.
# W1: the window kernel under the WATCHER (NoC sanitiser, waypoints) on a reduced scope: first sight of a hang, a watcher error or any differing byte, before the full run.
# REQUIRES scripts/ci/gdn_wy_block.py (the planned kernel; see docs/gdn-wy-probe.md "What remains"); without it the harness runs the baseline half and ends NO-DECISION, so
# the driver SKIPS this job unless the integration commit holds that file. A reduced scope never reads CONTINUE: this pass is for a watcher error, a hang and a causality or
# packing mismatch (KILL), not for the timing verdict.
# Duration (estimate): 20-40 min (container timeout 2 h; a hang trips the per-call watchdog, exit 3, then reset the target card only).
# Read: no watcher error or assert line; the GDN_WY verdict line; a KILL names the first failing case. STOP on a watcher error, a hang or a KILL.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-wy-probe-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/wy_probe/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--sections selftest,sram,causality,packing --regimes R1 --seeds 17 --commits 1,16,17,31 --users 2
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-wy-probe-1 WATCHER=1
